<title>CANADA: Canadian West Coast grain vessel loadings - CWB.</title>
<headline>Canadian West Coast grain vessel loadings - CWB.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Canadian Wheat Board reported seven grain vessels loading, 10 waiting and 12 due at the Canadian West Coast as of Tuesday, August 5.</p>
<p>The longest wait to load on the West Coast was 14 days.</p>
<p>West coast breakdown was as follows:</p>
<p>    Port	    Loading    Waiting	Due</p>
<p>    Vancouver	 6	   10	    12</p>
<p>    Prince Rupert   1	    0	     0</p>
<p>There were two ships loading on the East Coast, two waiting and one due next week.</p>
<p>There were two ships loading at Thunder Bay, none waiting, and five due.</p>
<p>One ship was due at Churchill.</p>
<p>((Gilbert Le Gras 204 947 3548))</p>
</text>
